*.db filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Byte-hashed provenance inputs must check out identically on every platform.
#
# `recordDigest()` in lib/stage2b-authored-record.ts hashes this file's RAW BYTES
# (fs.readFileSync with no encoding). That digest is stamped into the generated
# capability-policy.json as `_generatedFrom.record` and asserted by
# scripts/test-stage2b-workbook.ts. On a CRLF checkout the recomputed digest is
# 352cc55022a23d76 instead of the committed da826a3b199357f8, so the assertion
# fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the policy being wrong.
#
# Pinning the input to LF makes that digest checkout-invariant. The fix belongs
# HERE and never in regenerating capability-policy.json: regenerating would bake
# one machine's line endings into a committed artifact and break it for everyone
# whose checkout differs.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the single file the byte-hash inventory found, rather
# than a repo-wide `* text=auto`, which would rewrite 579 index entries for a
# defect that lives in one. The inventory is reproducible: exactly one call site
# hashes raw file bytes, lib/stage2b-authored-record.ts:209.
scripts/fixtures/operation-taxonomy/capability-answers.json text eol=lf
